ars back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 184% of normal in July to August, then just 36% in September to October. So far in 2026, January to February was 32% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 25957 had its driest year in 2005 at 57% of normal.</p>"}
